 # Grid Traversal and Data Structure Adaptation
-
-
 ## Overview
-This family encompasses methods that adapt the domain traversal and data structures of isosurface extraction to handle sparse, hierarchical, or multi-resolution volumetric data, avoiding the memory and computational costs of dense regular grids [G]. Unlike standard grid-based methods that iterate over fixed arrays, these techniques traverse octrees, sparse point sets, or adaptive mesh refinement (AMR) boundaries, dynamically gathering scalar values and generating geometry only where necessary [G]. They are distinguished from their siblings by their specific approach to handling topological discontinuities: [Marching Cubes with Octree](1259-marching-cubes-with-octree.md) relies on uniform node sizing to prevent cracks, [Sparse Marching Cubes](3825-sparse-marching-cubes.md) uses dynamic lookup for scattered points, [Hierarchical Marching Cubes Enumeration](5223-hierarchical-marching-cubes-enumeration.md) explicitly separates traversal logic for faces, edges, and vertices to ensure coherence, and [2D Stitching](10249-2d-stitching.md) generates stitch cells to bridge AMR level gaps without subdividing quadrilaterals.
-
